 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the 6 tests pass (the 4 that were already there plus the 2 I added). I only ran the test suite; I didn't write separate checks for the other spec changes.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` counting as not flagged and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `flags_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries, `dedupe_transcripts` now says it keeps the last record per id, and there is a new `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest against the spec turned up three more fixes.\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now returns `None` for empty groups, with keys sorted.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` now resets the count when a run breaks.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what a `flagged` value other than `1`, `0` or empty should do. I made `parse_transcript_log` raise `ValueError` with the line number for those, matching how it treats the other bad lines.\n\nI also made `flags_in_window` return `0` for a negative `days`, and `top_flagged_groups` return an empty list for a negative `n`. The spec doesn't cover either case.",
